    The error model is each catalogue's own: MUSE-DARK II uses its posterior sigma on log v_c and
    the 16-84 spread on log M*, plus 0.35 dex on the scaling-relation gas (Tacconi+20 molecular and
    NeutralUniverseMachine HI, whose own quoted scatter in log tau_HI is 0.8 dex) and 0.14 dex on R_e.
    RC100/MSA-3D/KROSS have no error columns in the tables on disk, so literature-typical values are
    used and are stated in the source; their rows are indicative, MUSE-DARK II's is not.
  [FAIL] k-hz-2 THE NOISE-FORWARD TEST, and it is the one that decides whether the census is a finding: MUSE-DARK II's violation fraction is compared with what its OWN quoted errors produce when the floor holds exactly.  The check fails if the observed fraction is NOT in excess of the noise   (MUSE-DARK II excess = 0.65 sigma over the noise expectation (>2 required); RC100 -0.41 sigma, SPARC degraded 1.59 sigma)

    ^ THIS FAILURE IS THE RESULT, and it is stated against the proposing stage's own interest: the
      pre-specified gate was 'observed fraction in excess of the noise by > 2 sigma => the census is
      a statement about galaxies'.  It is not met.  The 25.3% is what the catalogue's own error bars
      produce when the floor holds exactly, so K-C has no empirical content beyond measurement error.

    PART 2b -- WHICH galaxies violate?  Split by the stellar share of g_bar, f_star:
              f_star bin     N  N below    frac   median log(M_gas/M_*)
               0.00-0.05    12       12   1.000                    1.57
               0.05-0.15    19        6   0.316                    0.98
