      The five worst objects have f_star = 0.03, i.e. 97% of their catalogued baryonic mass is the
      NeutralUniverseMachine HI scaling relation extrapolated for a low-M*, low-SFR galaxy.  One of
      them (AS1063 952: log M* = 8.95, log M_bar = 10.54, magnification 19.8) is 1.17 dex below its
      own floor -- no mass calibration at any plausible level rescues it.
  [PASS] k-hz-2b THE DIAGNOSIS, and it is a check that can fail: if the census were about gravity or about redshift it would not care which COMPONENT supplies g_bar.  It does: the violators are the gas-scaling-relation-dominated objects, so the statistic is a meter for the assumed gas mass   (corr(f_star, violation) = -0.522; violators' median f_star = 0.053 against non-violators' 0.421)

